      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "DBD::File versions before 1.651 for Perl do not ensure the table file is not a symlink to an untrusted location.  The complete_table_name method builds the absolute table file path without checking whether the file is a symbolic link. A link inside the data directory can point to a table file at any path outside of the configured f_dir and f_dir_search directories.  Callers of file-based drivers can read or write files outside of the data directory.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
